Job Description:
We are a business based in Lagos currently looking to hire Customer Service Officers in developing Sales and Marketing experience, to work in our office from our office based close to Oshodi. You will be required to provide excellent customer support to our clients and also help with our Lead generation objectives.
Key Responsibilities
Deliver exceptional customer service and support through telephone, email, WhatsApp and social media channels.
Respond promptly, professionally, and courteously to customer enquiries, requests, complaints, and feedback.
Build and maintain positive relationships with existing and prospective customers to ensure a high level of customer satisfaction.
Identify and research potential clients, business opportunities, and target markets under the guidance of senior team members.
Generate and qualify leads through online research, telephone outreach, email campaigns, referrals, and other approved lead generation activities.
Maintain accurate records of customer interactions, enquiries, leads, and follow-up activities within the company systems.
Assist in preparing and sending professional emails, proposals, marketing materials, and follow-up communications to prospective clients.
Support business development activities by booking appointments, arranging meetings, and maintaining contact with prospective clients.
Learn and effectively use telephone scripts, customer engagement techniques, and lead generation processes to achieve agreed objectives.
Conduct market and competitor research to identify trends, opportunities, and potential customers.
Monitor and report on customer service activities, lead generation performance, and business development progress.
Work independently while managing assigned tasks, priorities, and deadlines with minimal supervision.
Collaborate with colleagues to improve customer experience, service delivery, lead generation effectiveness, and overall business performance.
Meet agreed customer service, lead generation, and performance targets while maintaining high professional standards.
Participate actively in training and development activities to improve communication, sales, customer service, and business development skills.
Requirements
Excellent verbal and written communication skills.
Strong customer service and relationship management abilities.
Proven ability to generate leads and develop new business opportunities.
Good understanding of sales, marketing, and customer engagement strategies.
Ability to work independently, take initiative, and solve problems proactively.
Strong organizational skills with attention to detail.
Proficiency in Microsoft Office, Google Workspace, and online communication tools.
Ability to meet targets and perform effectively in a results-driven environment.
Skills:
A result oriented Individual with a flexible approach to work;
A fast learner who is keen to grow their marketing skills;
An effective and confident communicator with the ability to influence situations;
Very good level of English Language - both written and spoken;
Excellent Telephone handling skills;
Excellent Computer Literacy & Record Keeping Skills;
Excellent Administrative and Organizational skills
Possess an excellent personal drive and self-motivational skills;
Strong orientation to achieving team's goals and targets set;
Willingness to learn and develop;
Team player open to share knowledge and to support your colleagues;
Call Centre Experience will be an advantage;
Professional attitude and orientation to details;
Knowledge of Marketing Principles & Techniques;
Knowledge of using LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram;
Knowledge of CRM Applications;

Overall Administration
Provide hospitality to guests and create a welcoming environment;
Manage databases and filing system for the Principal's office;
Coordinate with the admin team to arrange domestic and international travels and logistics for the Principal; Liaise with the office assistants to ensure that the Principal's office is clean at all times and escalate utility faults as appropriate;
Liaise with the admin team to provide event management support including coordination of meeting logistics;
Ensure stock up of utility supplies for the Principal's office and manage refreshments, supplies and food orders;
Manage audits, advances and retirement of expense reports for the Principal; Other duties as assigned.
Required competencies
Core requirements
Compelling evidence of interest in and commitment to the mission of SCIDaR;
Ability to effectively manage relationships with Solina's internal and external stakeholders;
Possess strong communication skills and team-oriented interpersonal skills
Proficiency in the use of Microsoft office package (Word, Excel and PowerPoint);
Ability to execute work in a diverse, fast paced environment with people at all organizational levels
Demonstrate professionalism, sensitivity, a high level of confidentiality and a positive attitude at all times
Ability to make appropriate, informed decisions regarding priorities and available time;
Possess excellent organisational skills and attention to details;
Ability to work under pressure and time constraints and easily adapt to ever-changing conditions;
Results-oriented performer, experienced in developing and tracking self and team with clear KPIs.
Education and Experience
Academic training: Minimum of Bachelors' degree from a reputable university;
Experience: Minimum of five (5) years of progressive experience in office management systems and procedures.
Prior experience as an Executive Assistant or Administrative Officer in a reputable organisation is a plus.

Company Details:
The philosophy of the polytechnic is embodied in her MOTTO which is "SKILL FOR TECHNOLOGYICAL FREEDOM". The philosophy is principally aimed at inculcating in students and staff the discipline of hard-work to be able to acquire both the practical and theoretical skills necessary for self re...read moreliance. The Logo shows the local pottery/ceramics, one of the mankind’s earliest technologies. Inside the pot with a gear wheel stopper are ears of rice an expression of the link between agriculture technology and engineering technology. The entire conception is a symbol of motion to modern technology. The objectives of the Polytechnic are in keeping with the Federal Government policy on Technical Education, which broadly stated, are:

 To provide trained manpower in applied Science, Technology and Commerce particularly on sub-professional grades;
 To provide the technical knowledge and vocational skills necessary for agricultural, industrial, commercial and economic development;
 To provide people who can apply scientific knowledge to the improvement and solution of environmental problems for the use and convenience of man;
 To give an introduction to professional studies in engineering and other Technologies;
 To give training and impart the necessary skills leading to the production of craftsman, technicians and other skilled personnel who will be enterprising and self-reliant; and
 To enable our young men and women to have an intelligent understanding of the increasing complexity of technology.
 Akanu Ibiam Federal Polytechnic, Unwana in its 30 years of existence from October 1981 till date has not only lived and performed creditably within expectation but well above board.

